History:

A long time ago, Malcolm Ryan put out a patch that made statues display
in tty mode as the letter of the right monster rather than a backtick.
The problem with that patch is that it broke save file compatibility
and it was very large and thus hard to maintain for new versions of
nethack.  I have written a new, short, patch that doesn't break save
files.  That means Hearse will work...

Effect:

When you use tty mode, statue glyphs are displayed with the letter of
the appropriate monster rather than a backtick.  The color is grey,
like a statue.  There is no change in any other display mode.  There
are no changes to any internal structures, so save files are 100%
compatible.

How it works:

In mapglyph.c, when a statue glyph is being changed into a letter, we
detect if the glyph is a statue, and if so we show the right letter.
Hallucination and mimics are taken care of.

Patch:

Insert the following lines around line 137 in mapglyph.c; the context
is shown below.

--- BEGIN PATCH
       if ( offset == STATUE)
          if ( ! Hallucination  && OBJ_AT(x,y)
                   && vobj_at(x,y)->otyp == STATUE)
              ch =  monsyms[(int)mons[vobj_at(x,y)->corpsenm].mlet];
         else
              ch = monsyms[(int)mons[0].mlet];
--- END PATCH

These lines go right after the following code

        if (offset == BOULDER && iflags.bouldersym) ch =
iflags.bouldersym;
        else ch = oc_syms[(int)objects[offset].oc_class];

and right before

        #ifdef ROGUE_COLOR


Minor bug:
Nethack doesn't have a separate glyph for hallucinated statues versus
regular statues. Thus a hallucinated statue that is over top of a real
staute is identified in vanilla nethack (by the ; key) as the correct
type of statue, since the game has no way to tell that the glyph in
that location is due to hallucination.  Under this patch, if you
hallucinate a staute over a real statue, it will show up as an `a`
(matching the description) but sometime after you stop hallucinating it
will revert to the true glyph even if you didn't see it again.  This
only happens if the hallucinated staute is on top of a real statue,
which doesn't happen very often.  It doesn't happen if you hallucinate
a statue over a non-statue glyph.

This bug is hard to detect with vanilla nethack -- it only manifests
itself in the poor descriptions given by the ; key.  Essentially, it is
just impossible to hallucinate a different statue on top of a real
statue in vanilla nethack, since two statues are only distinguished by
their descriptions.



